   "action": "Action: M/S/C (Ishii/Humbert) to suspend the rules and establish a three-hour public comment period for the agenda item with time for both in-person and online speakers. Vote: Ayes – Kesarwani, Taplin, Bartlett, Tregub, O’Keefe, Blackaby, Humbert, Ishii; Noes – None; Abstain – Lunaparra. Action: M/S/C (Lunaparra/Ishii) to suspend the rules and extend the public comment period for an additional hour. Vote: Ayes – Kesarwani, Bartlett, Tregub, O’Keefe, Blackaby, Lunaparra, Ishii; Noes – Taplin; Abstain – Humbert. Action: M/S/C (Ishii/Lunaparra) to suspend the rules and extend the meeting to 12:00 a.m. Vote: All Ayes. Action Calendar – New Business Action: M/S/Failed (Ishii/Blackaby) to adopt the resolution submitted by Mayor Ishii and Councilmember Bartlett in Supplemental Communications Packet #2 titled “Resolution Reaffirming the City of Berkeley’s Commitment to Combatting Hate, Supporting a Lasting Peace Between Israel and Gaza, Opposing a U.S. Occupation of Gaza and Respecting Freedom ‘f Speech.” Vote: Ayes – Bartlett, Tregub, Lunaparra, Ishii; Noes – Blackaby; Abstain – Kesarwani, Taplin, O’Keefe, Humbert. Action: 197 speakers. M/S/Carried (Lunaparra/Ishii) to adopt Resolution No. 71,726–N.S. submitted by Councilmember Taplin in Supplemental Communications Packet #2 titled “Reaffirming Berkeley’s Commitment to Peace, at Home and Abroad.” Vote: Ayes – Kesarwani, Taplin, Tregub, O’Keefe, Blackaby, Humbert, Ishii; Noes – Lunaparra; Abstain – Bartlett.",
